# §3306. Definitions

> Module Section3306

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using SaraPredicates as P
> Using Section7703 as S7703
> Using Section152 as S152

Port of `section3306.pl`, the definitions chapter 23 hangs on: who is an
**employer** (a), what counts as **wages** (b), and what counts as
**employment** (c). §3301 imposes the unemployment tax on (a) × (b) × (c), and
`tax/3` adds that to §1, so this module is the last one the corpus needs.

Three things make it unlike the income-tax sections.

**It is arithmetic over multisets, not a yes/no test.** §3301 sums wages, and
`sum_list` over a `findall` counts *solutions*, not facts: a remuneration with
two `amount_` rows contributes twice, and a disjunction that both branches
satisfy contributes twice again. Every generator here is therefore a list whose
length is the Prolog's solution count, never a set.

**It counts days and weeks.** (a)(1)(B) and (a)(2)(B) want ten days "each in a
different calendar week", which SARA answers with `format_time/3` `%W`. That is
reproduced exactly in `week_of` below, including the fact that the week key
carries no year, so week 5 of one year and week 5 of the next collide.

**It is the only section with a genuine dependency cycle inside itself**, since
(c) excludes agricultural labor unless (a)(2) is satisfied, and (a)(2) asks (c)
which days were worked. See "Cutting the two cycles" below.

## Helpers

```catala-metadata
## `is_before/2` guards on `nonvar` for both arguments, so a comparison against
## an unbound date *fails* rather than succeeding vacuously. Every query
## argument that Prolog may leave unbound is an `optional` here, and this is
## what "unbound" costs.
declaration ent_ok content boolean
  depends on want content optional of W.Entity, got content W.Entity
  equals
    match want with pattern
    -- Absent: true
    -- Present content e: e.id = got.id

## The multiset of role fillers matching a (possibly unbound) query argument.
## Its length is the number of ways the Prolog goal succeeds.
declaration ent_hits content list of W.Entity
  depends on want content optional of W.Entity, got content list of W.Entity
  equals list of g among got such that (ent_ok of want, g)

## `purpose_(E,P)`, counting the universally quantified facts the corpus
## carries -- `purpose_(_, "agricultural labor")` applies to every event.
declaration purpose_hits content list of W.Purpose
  depends on world content W.World, ev content W.Event, p content W.Purpose
  equals
    (list of x among ev.purposes such that x = p)
    ++ (list of x among world.universal_purposes such that x = p)

declaration has_purpose content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, ev content W.Event, p content W.Purpose
  equals (number of (purpose_hits of world, ev, p)) > 0

## `type_(E,T)`. type_ shares purpose_'s vocabulary; unlike purpose_ it has no
## universally quantified rows.
declaration has_type content boolean
  depends on ev content W.Event, p content W.Purpose
  equals ev.types contains p

## (c)(1) and (c)(2) both ask "is this agricultural labor / domestic service",
## reading purpose_ *or* type_. As a disjunction each side counts separately
## where multiplicity matters.
declaration agri_hits content list of W.Purpose
  depends on world content W.World, ev content W.Event
  equals
    (purpose_hits of world, ev, W.Purpose.AgriculturalLabor)
    ++ (list of x among ev.types such that x = W.Purpose.AgriculturalLabor)

declaration is_agricultural content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, ev content W.Event
  equals (number of (agri_hits of world, ev)) > 0

declaration is_domestic content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, ev content W.Event
  equals
    (has_type of ev, W.Purpose.DomesticService)
    or (has_purpose of world, ev, W.Purpose.DomesticService)

## The same two tests for a service named only by id. A case that injects a
## clause for `s3306_c/5` names services the event base never mentions, and
## `purpose_(Service,"agricultural labor")` still succeeds for them when the
## case carries the universally quantified row `purpose_(_,"agricultural
## labor")` -- which is exactly how `s3306_a_2_B_pos` is written.
declaration is_agricultural_id content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, e content W.Entity
  equals
    (world.universal_purposes contains W.Purpose.AgriculturalLabor)
    or (exists ev among world.events such that
          ev.ident.id = e.id and (is_agricultural of world, ev))

declaration is_domestic_id content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, e content W.Entity
  equals
    (world.universal_purposes contains W.Purpose.DomesticService)
    or (exists ev among world.events such that
          ev.ident.id = e.id and (is_domestic of world, ev))

## The event with this identifier, if the world has one. Several §3306 queries
## name a service or a payment directly.
declaration event_named content optional of W.Event
  depends on world content W.World, id content W.Entity
  equals List.first_element of (list of e among world.events such that e.ident.id = id.id)

## `\+ end_(E,_) ; ( end_(E,T), is_before(Day,T) )` -- an open window, read at
## a day that may itself be unbound.
declaration open_at content boolean
  depends on starts content list of date, ends content list of date,
             at content optional of date
  equals
    match at with pattern
    -- Absent: false
    -- Present content d:
        (exists s among starts such that s <= d)
        and ((number of ends) = 0 or (exists e among ends such that d <= e))

## The `%W` week number SARA gets out of `format_time/3`: weeks start on
## Monday, and the days before the year's first Monday are week 0.
##
## `day_to_stamp/2` builds the stamp from `date(Y,M,D+1,0,0,0,0,-,-)`, i.e. UTC
## midnight of the *next* day, and `format_time/3` then renders it in local
## time. On any timezone west of UTC -- which is where the gold was produced --
## the two shifts cancel and the week is that of the original day. This
## reproduces that, and `sara_scripts/DEVIATIONS.md` records the dependence.
declaration week_of content integer
  depends on d content date
  equals
    let yday equals integer of ((d - (Date.first_day_of_year of d)) / 1 day) in
    let monday_index equals
      (match (Date.day_of_week of d) with pattern
       -- Monday: 0
       -- Tuesday: 1
       -- Wednesday: 2
       -- Thursday: 3
       -- Friday: 4
       -- Saturday: 5
       -- Sunday: 6) in
    integer of ((decimal of (yday + 7 - monday_index)) / 7.0)

## `list_to_set/2`, which keeps the first occurrence of each element.
declaration dedup_dates content list of date
  depends on l content list of date
  equals
    combine all x among l in acc initially []
    with (if acc contains x then acc else acc ++ [x])

declaration dedup_ints content list of integer
  depends on l content list of integer
  equals
    combine all x among l in acc initially []
    with (if acc contains x then acc else acc ++ [x])

declaration dedup_entities content list of W.Entity
  depends on l content list of W.Entity
  equals
    combine all x among l in acc initially []
    with (if (exists a among acc such that a.id = x.id) then acc else acc ++ [x])

declaration flatten_entities content list of W.Entity
  depends on nested content list of list of W.Entity
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

declaration flatten_money content list of money
  depends on nested content list of list of money
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

declaration flatten_dates content list of date
  depends on nested content list of list of date
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

## One row of a `findall` that collects an amount together with the employee
## and service it was paid for -- §3306(a)(2)(A), (a)(3) and (c)(1)(A)(i) all
## collect that shape.
declaration structure AgriRow:
  data amount content money
  data employee content W.Entity
  data service content W.Entity

declaration flatten_agri content list of AgriRow
  depends on nested content list of list of AgriRow
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

## `n` copies of one solution. Several goals in a §3306 conjunction can match
## more than one fact, and `sum_list` over a `findall` counts every one of
## them; collapsing to a set would understate the wages.
declaration repeat_agri content list of AgriRow
  depends on r content AgriRow, n content integer
  equals map each i among (List.sequence of 1, (n + 1)) to r

## `(\+ means_(P,_)) ; means_(P,"cash")` -- the number of ways a payment
## counts as made in cash.
declaration cash_ways content integer
  depends on pay content W.Event
  equals
    if (number of pay.media) = 0
    then 1
    else (number of (list of m among pay.media such that m = W.Medium.Cash))
```

## Places and countries

`s3306_c_A` asks whether a service was performed in the United States, and it
answers by chasing `location_` to a place and `country_` from that place. A
`Place` is an enumeration here, so getting from a place back to the entity that
carries its `country_` rows takes one step.

```catala-metadata
## The entity a place names, where the world has facts about it. `Usa` is the
## interned atom "usa", which the emitter tags.
declaration entity_of_place content optional of W.Entity
  depends on world content W.World, g content W.Place
  equals
    match g with pattern
    -- NamedPlace content e: Present content e
    -- Usa:
        List.first_element of
          (map each ev among
            (list of e among world.events
             such that e.ident.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity)
           to ev.ident)
    -- PrivateHome: Absent
    -- LocalCollegeClub: Absent
    -- LocalCollegeFraternityChapter: Absent
    -- LocalCollegeSororityChapter: Absent
    -- UnitedStatesGovernment: Absent

## `country_(G,C)` for a place.
declaration countries_of_place content list of W.Entity
  depends on world content W.World, g content W.Place
  equals
    match (entity_of_place of world, g) with pattern
    -- Absent: []
    -- Present content e:
        flatten_entities of
          (map each ev among
            (list of x among world.events such that x.ident.id = e.id)
           to ev.countries)

## `G == "usa"`, the atom comparison the Prolog falls back on when the place
## has no `country_` row at all.
declaration place_is_usa content boolean
  depends on g content W.Place
  equals
    match g with pattern
    -- Usa: true
    -- NamedPlace content e: e.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity
    -- PrivateHome: false
    -- LocalCollegeClub: false
    -- LocalCollegeFraternityChapter: false
    -- LocalCollegeSororityChapter: false
    -- UnitedStatesGovernment: false

## `((country_(G,C), C=="usa") ; (\+ country_(G,_), G=="usa"))`.
declaration place_in_usa content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, g content W.Place
  equals
    (exists c among (countries_of_place of world, g)
     such that c.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity)
    or ((number of (countries_of_place of world, g)) = 0
        and (place_is_usa of g))

## The same test with the sign flipped, as (B) writes it: a place that is in
## some country other than the USA, or that is not the atom "usa".
declaration place_outside_usa content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, g content W.Place
  equals
    (exists c among (countries_of_place of world, g)
     such that c.tag != W.EntityTag.UsaEntity)
    or ((number of (countries_of_place of world, g)) = 0
        and not (place_is_usa of g))

## `location_(Service,G) ; (\+ location_(Service,_), G = "usa")` -- the places
## a service was performed at, defaulting to the USA.
declaration places_of content list of W.Place
  depends on ev content W.Event
  equals if (number of ev.places) = 0 then [W.Place.Usa] else ev.places
```

```catala-metadata
## `location_(E, X)` where X is an entity rather than one of the named places.
declaration place_is content boolean
  depends on g content W.Place, e content W.Entity
  equals
    match g with pattern
    -- NamedPlace content x: x.id = e.id
    -- Usa: e.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity
    -- PrivateHome: false
    -- LocalCollegeClub: false
    -- LocalCollegeFraternityChapter: false
    -- LocalCollegeSororityChapter: false
    -- UnitedStatesGovernment: e.tag = W.EntityTag.UnitedStatesGovernmentEntity

declaration place_ok content boolean
  depends on g content W.Place, want content optional of W.Entity
  equals
    match want with pattern
    -- Absent: true
    -- Present content e: place_is of g, e

## The four places §3306(c)(2) names as private domestic settings.
declaration is_private_setting content boolean
  depends on g content W.Place
  equals
    g = W.Place.PrivateHome or g = W.Place.LocalCollegeClub
    or g = W.Place.LocalCollegeFraternityChapter
    or g = W.Place.LocalCollegeSororityChapter
```

## (c) Employment — the exclusions

Paragraphs (5) through (21) each take a service back *out* of "employment".
Every one of them is a plain existence test, so each gets a scope reporting
`holds`, and `s3306_c` requires all of them to fail.

Four of them — (5), (10), (13) and (21) — test a date against `Workday`.
`is_before/2` demands both arguments be bound, so when the caller left `Workday`
unbound each of those tests *fails*, and the service is not excluded. That is
not a rounding of the Prolog: it is what the Prolog does, and it is the reason
`s3306_c` behaves differently depending on whether its caller named a day.

### (6) The United States Government, and (7) a State

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ExclUsGovernment:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  ## s3306_c_6/1
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope ExclState:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  ## s3306_c_7/2
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope ExclForeignGovernment:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  ## s3306_c_11/2
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope ExclInternationalOrganization:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  ## s3306_c_16/2
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope ExclUsGovernment:
  ## The Prolog does not require `service_(Service)` here, only `patient_/2`.
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             p.tag = W.EntityTag.UnitedStatesGovernmentEntity)

scope ExclState:
  ## `atom_prefix(Employer,"state of ")`, resolved by the emitter into a tag.
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             (ent_ok of employer, p) and p.tag = W.EntityTag.StateEntity)

scope ExclForeignGovernment:
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service
      and (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             (ent_ok of employer, p)
             and p.tag = W.EntityTag.ForeignGovernmentEntity)

scope ExclInternationalOrganization:
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service
      and (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             (ent_ok of employer, p)
             and (exists io among world.events such that
                    io.kinds contains W.EventKind.InternationalOrganization
                    and io.agents contains p))
```

### (21) A person committed to a penal institution

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ExclPenalInstitution:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  ## s3306_c_21/4
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope ExclPenalInstitution:
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists a among ev.agents such that
             (ent_ok of employee, a)
             and (exists inc among world.events such that
                    inc.kinds contains W.EventKind.Incarceration
                    and inc.agents contains a
                    and (exists jail among inc.patients such that
                           exists pi among world.events such that
                             pi.kinds contains W.EventKind.PenalInstitution
                             and pi.agents contains jail)
                    and (open_at of inc.starts, inc.ends, workday)))
```

### (13) A student nurse

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ExclStudentNurse:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  ## s3306_c_13/4
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope ExclStudentNurse:
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             (ent_ok of employer, p)
             # the employer is a nurses' training school or a hospital
             and (exists h among world.events such that
                    (h.kinds contains W.EventKind.NursesTrainingSchool
                     or h.kinds contains W.EventKind.Hospital)
                    and h.agents contains p))
      and (exists a among ev.agents such that
             (ent_ok of employee, a)
             # enrolled at, and attending classes at, *some* nurses' training
             # school -- not necessarily the employer, as the Prolog writes it
             and (exists nts among world.events such that
                    nts.kinds contains W.EventKind.NursesTrainingSchool
                    and (exists school among nts.agents such that
                           (exists en among world.events such that
                              en.kinds contains W.EventKind.Enrollment
                              and en.agents contains a
                              and en.patients contains school
                              and (open_at of en.starts, en.ends, workday))
                           and (exists ac among world.events such that
                                  ac.kinds contains W.EventKind.AttendingClasses
                                  and ac.agents contains a
                                  and (exists g among ac.places such that
                                         place_is of g, school)
                                  and (open_at of ac.starts, ac.ends, workday)))))
```

### (10) Students, their spouses, and hospital patients

(A)(i) is the student test; (A)(ii) lets a student's spouse inherit it, which is
the one place §3306 reaches back into §7703 and so into §152.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Student:
  input world content W.World
  input student content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  ## Which people satisfy the test, so (A) can compare them with the employee.
  output students content list of W.Entity
  ## s3306_c_10_A_i/3
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope StudentSpouse:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input spouse content W.Entity
  input student content W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  ## s3306_c_10_A_ii/3
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope ExclStudent:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  ## s3306_c_10_A/4
  output holds_a content boolean
  ## s3306_c_10_B/4
  output holds_b content boolean
  ## s3306_c_10/4
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope Student:
  definition students equals
    dedup_entities of
      (flatten_entities of
        (map each en among
          (list of e among world.events
           such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Enrollment
                     and (open_at of e.starts, e.ends, workday))
         to (list of st among en.agents such that
               (ent_ok of student, st)
               # enrolled at the employer ...
               and (exists p among en.patients such that ent_ok of employer, p)
               # ... and regularly attending classes there
               and (exists ac among world.events such that
                      ac.kinds contains W.EventKind.AttendingClasses
                      and ac.agents contains st
                      and (exists g among ac.places such that
                             (place_ok of g, employer)
                             and (exists p among en.patients such that
                                    place_is of g, p))
                      and (open_at of ac.starts, ac.ends, workday)))))

  definition holds equals (number of students) > 0

scope StudentSpouse:
  ## `s7703(Student,Spouse,Marriage,Year)` -- the marriage has to be reported,
  ## not just the fact of being married, because the window test below reads
  ## its start and end. `Year` comes from the workday.
  definition holds equals
    match workday with pattern
    -- Absent: false
    -- Present content d:
        (exists sp among
           (output of S7703.MaritalStatus with {
              -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: student
              -- taxable_year: Date.get_year of d
              -- qualifying_dependants:
                   (output of S152.QualifyingChildrenOf with {
                      -- injections: injections -- world: world
                      -- taxpayer: student
                      -- taxable_year: Date.get_year of d
                      -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                      -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                      -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).children }).spouses
         such that sp.id = spouse.id)
        and (exists c among
               (output of S7703.MaritalStatusA with {
                  -- world: world -- taxpayer: student
                  -- taxable_year: Date.get_year of d }).candidates
             such that
               c.spouse.id = spouse.id
               # `\+ start_(M,_) ; is_before(Start,Workday)`, and likewise the end
               and ((number of c.marriage.starts) = 0
                    or (exists s among c.marriage.starts such that s <= d))
               and ((number of c.marriage.ends) = 0
                    or (exists e among c.marriage.ends such that d <= e)))
        # and the spouse is themselves enrolled somewhere -- `Employer` is
        # left unbound at this call site, so any institution will do
        and (output of Student with {
               -- world: world -- student: Present content spouse
               -- employer: Absent -- workday: workday }).holds

scope ExclStudent:
  definition holds_a equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             (ent_ok of employer, p)
             and (exists ei among world.events such that
                    ei.kinds contains W.EventKind.EducationalInstitution
                    and ei.agents contains p)
             and (exists a among ev.agents such that
                    (ent_ok of employee, a)
                    and (exists st among
                           (output of Student with {
                              -- world: world -- student: Absent
                              -- employer: Present content p
                              -- workday: workday }).students
                         such that
                           st.id = a.id
                           or (output of StudentSpouse with {
                                 -- world: world -- injections: injections
                                 -- child_of: child_of
                                 -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                                 -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                                 -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                                 -- spouse: a -- student: st
                                 -- workday: workday }).holds)))

  definition holds_b equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service
      and (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists p among ev.patients such that
             (ent_ok of employer, p)
             and (exists h among world.events such that
                    h.kinds contains W.EventKind.Hospital and h.agents contains p)
             and (exists a among ev.agents such that
                    (ent_ok of employee, a)
                    and (exists mp among world.events such that
                           mp.kinds contains W.EventKind.MedicalPatient
                           and mp.agents contains a
                           and mp.patients contains p
                           and (open_at of mp.starts, mp.ends, workday))))

  definition holds equals holds_a or holds_b
```

### (5) Service within the family

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ExclFamily:
  input world content W.World
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  #  `agent_(Service,Employee)` and `patient_(Service,Employer)`: the person
  #  doing the work and the person they do it for. Named after the roles they
  #  read rather than after the statute, because (A) and (B) swap which of the
  #  two has to be the child.
  input agent content optional of W.Entity
  input patient content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  # s3306_c_5_A/4
  output holds_a content boolean
  # s3306_c_5_B/4
  output holds_b content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope ExclFamily:
  definition holds_a equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service
      and (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists a among ev.agents such that
             (ent_ok of agent, a)
             and (exists p among ev.patients such that
                    (ent_ok of patient, p)
                    and (
                      # the employer is a child of the employee ...
                      (exists k among child_of such that
                         k.subject.id = p.id and k.object.id = a.id)
                      # ... or they are married, on the workday
                      or (exists m among world.events such that
                            m.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
                            and m.agents contains p and m.agents contains a
                            and p.id != a.id
                            and (open_at of m.starts, m.ends, workday)))))

  definition holds_b equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service
      and (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (exists a among ev.agents such that
             (ent_ok of agent, a)
             and (exists p among ev.patients such that
                    (ent_ok of patient, p)
                    and (exists k among child_of such that
                           k.subject.id = a.id and k.object.id = p.id)
                    and (match workday with pattern
                         -- Absent: false
                         -- Present content d:
                             exists b among world.events such that
                               b.kinds contains W.EventKind.Birth
                               and b.agents contains a
                               and (exists dob among b.starts such that
                                      d < dob + 7671 day))))

  definition holds equals holds_a or holds_b
```

`s3306_c_5_B` reads the twenty-first birthday as `date(Y, M, D + 7671)`, which
SWI normalises: 7671 days past the date of birth. Twenty-one years is 7,670.25
days, so this is the day of birth plus 21 years give or take a day, and the
comparison is strict.

### (1) Agricultural labor

```catala-metadata
declaration scope AgriculturalAlien:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  # s3306_c_1_B/2, which is itself a negation: the labor is *not* performed by
  # an alien admitted to the United States to perform it.
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope AgriculturalWages:
  input world content W.World
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input caly content integer
  # The `(Amount, Employee, Service)` triples the findall collects, in order.
  output rows content list of AgriRow
  output total content money
  # The second and third findalls project the same triples, so the employee
  # list a case may name is this projection, duplicates and all.
  output employees content list of W.Entity
  # s3306_c_1_A_i/5
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope AgriculturalAlien:
  definition holds equals
    not (exists ev among world.events such that
           (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
           and (is_agricultural of world, ev)
           and (exists cz among world.events such that
                  cz.kinds contains W.EventKind.Citizenship
                  and (exists person among cz.agents such that
                         (exists country among cz.patients such that
                            country.tag != W.EntityTag.UsaEntity)
                         and (exists mg among world.events such that
                                mg.kinds contains W.EventKind.Migration
                                and mg.agents contains person
                                and (exists dest among mg.destinations such that
                                       place_is_usa of dest)
                                and (has_purpose of world, mg,
                                       W.Purpose.AgriculturalLabor)))))

scope AgriculturalWages:
  # `findall(Amount, (payment for agricultural service in Caly or Caly-1))`,
  # then `sum_list` and a $20,000 threshold. The window spans two calendar
  # years: from the first day of the preceding year to the last of this one.
  #
  # The nesting is the Prolog's conjunction, in its order, so the list length
  # is the solution count rather than the number of distinct payments. Each
  # goal that can match more than one fact multiplies the row.
  definition rows equals
    flatten_agri of
      (map each pay among
        (list of e among world.events such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Payment)
       to (flatten_agri of
            (map each er among (ent_hits of employer, pay.agents)
             to (flatten_agri of
                  (map each ee among pay.patients
                   to (flatten_agri of
                        (map each svc among
                          (list of s among world.events
                           such that s.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service)
                         to (flatten_agri of
                              (map each amt among pay.amounts
                               to (repeat_agri of
                                    AgriRow { -- amount: amt -- employee: ee
                                              -- service: svc.ident },
                               ((number of (list of a among svc.agents
                                            such that a.id = ee.id))
                                * (number of (list of q among svc.patients
                                              such that q.id = er.id))
                                * (number of (agri_hits of world, svc))
                                * (number of (purpose_hits of world, pay,
                                     (W.Purpose.PurposeEntity content svc.ident)))
                                * (number of (list of t among pay.starts such that
                                     (W.first_day_year of (caly - 1)) <= t
                                     and t <= (W.last_day_year of caly)))
                                * (cash_ways of pay))))))))))))

  definition total equals Money.sum of (map each r among rows to r.amount)

  definition employees equals map each r among rows to r.employee

  definition holds equals total >= $20,000
```

## Cutting the two cycles

Subsection (c) excludes agricultural labor unless (a)(2) is satisfied, and
(a)(2) asks (c) which days were worked. It excludes domestic service unless
(a)(3) is satisfied, and (a)(3) asks (b) for wages, which asks (c). Both are
cycles Catala rejects statically, and both are cut here — the first by the
Prolog's own guard, the second by measurement.

**(c)(1)(A) → (a)(2)(B) → (c).** `s3306_c_1_A` opens with `nonvar(Caly)`, and
`s3306_a_2_is_day_of_employment` calls `s3306_c` with the calendar year
*unbound*. So the inner call can never re-enter (c)(1)(A): the recursion is one
level deep by construction. `EmploymentInner` below is that inner level, and it
is a separate scope precisely so the dependency graph stays a DAG.
Instrumenting the Prolog over all 376 cases traverses this edge 30 times, in 6
cases, and never nested — which is what that guard predicts.

**(c)(2) → (a)(3) → (b) → (c).** Nothing cuts this one, and with `Caly` unbound
`s3306_a_3` raises an instantiation error rather than failing. The same
instrumentation traverses the edge **zero** times: (c)(2) also demands the
service be located in a private home or a college club, and no live case has a
service that is both. (The two cases that would test it, `s3306_c_2_pos` and
`s3306_c_2_neg`, are the corpus's two inert files — an unterminated clause
swallows the query.) So `s3306_c_2` here is its guard alone, which is the
stricter reading: it excludes a service the full test might have kept.

```catala-metadata
## One solution of `s3306_c/5`. `workday` and `caly` travel with the row
## because a case may inject a *rule* for `s3306_c/5` that binds them, and
## (a)(1)(B) and (a)(2)(B) then count the days it yields.
declaration structure Emp:
  data service content W.Entity
  data employer content W.Entity
  data employee content W.Entity
  data workday content optional of date
  data caly content optional of integer

declaration flatten_emp content list of Emp
  depends on nested content list of list of Emp
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

## An argument recovered from an injected row, falling back on what the query
## asked for when the row left that position a don't-care.
declaration ent_from content W.Entity
  depends on got content optional of W.Entity, want content optional of W.Entity
  equals
    match got with pattern
    -- Present content e: e
    -- Absent:
        (match want with pattern
         -- Present content e: e
         -- Absent: W.Entity { -- id: -1 -- tag: W.EntityTag.PlainEntity })

## The match key for a (possibly unbound) entity argument.
declaration key_of content integer
  depends on want content optional of W.Entity
  equals
    match want with pattern
    -- Absent: -1
    -- Present content e: e.id

declaration date_key_of content integer
  depends on want content optional of date
  equals
    match want with pattern
    -- Absent: -1
    -- Present content d: 2000000 + (integer of ((d - |0001-01-01|) / 1 day)) + 1

declaration num_key_of content integer
  depends on want content optional of integer
  equals
    match want with pattern
    -- Absent: -1
    -- Present content n: W.num_key of n
```

The `+ 1` in `date_key_of` is the difference between Catala's day count from
`0001-01-01` and Python's `date.toordinal()`, which the emitter uses; the two
differ by one because `toordinal` is 1-based.

## (c)(A) and (c)(B): where the service was performed

(A) keeps service performed in the United States; (B) keeps service performed
abroad by a US citizen for an American employer. Both are generators, and their
solution *count* is what §3301 sums over, so each way a goal can match is one
row rather than one flag.

(B) has a mode artifact worth naming. `Location` is unbound at every call site,
so `country_(Location,Country), Country \== "usa"` ranges over every
`country_` fact in the world — it never looks at where *this* service was
performed. And when the world holds no `country_` facts at all, the second
branch succeeds with `Location` still unbound, so `Location \== "usa"` compares
a free variable against an atom and is true. Both are reproduced.

```catala-metadata
declaration repeat_emp content list of Emp
  depends on e content Emp, n content integer
  equals map each i among (List.sequence of 1, (n + 1)) to e

## `((country_(G,C), C=="usa") ; (\+ country_(G,_), G=="usa"))`, counted.
declaration usa_ways content integer
  depends on world content W.World, g content W.Place
  equals
    (number of (list of c among (countries_of_place of world, g)
                such that c.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity))
    + (if (number of (countries_of_place of world, g)) = 0 and (place_is_usa of g)
       then 1 else 0)

## Every entity carrying a `country_` row, once per row.
declaration country_rows content list of W.Entity
  depends on world content W.World
  equals
    flatten_entities of
      (map each ev among world.events to (map each c among ev.countries to ev.ident))

## Is there an unemployment compensation agreement between the USA and this
## place? With `Location` unbound the third goal matches any agent at all.
declaration uca_with content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, loc content optional of W.Entity
  equals
    exists ag among world.events such that
      ag.kinds contains W.EventKind.UnemploymentCompensationAgreement
      and (exists a among ag.agents such that a.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity)
      and (exists a among ag.agents such that ent_ok of loc, a)

## The ways (B)'s location test can succeed.
declaration foreign_ways content integer
  depends on world content W.World
  equals
    (number of
      (list of ev among world.events such that
         (exists c among ev.countries such that c.tag != W.EntityTag.UsaEntity)
         and not (uca_with of world, (Present content ev.ident))))
    + (if (number of (country_rows of world)) = 0
          and not (uca_with of world, Absent)
       then 1 else 0)

## `american_employer_(X), agent_(X,Employer)`, counted.
declaration american_employer_ways content integer
  depends on world content W.World, employer content W.Entity
  equals
    Integer.sum of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events
         such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.AmericanEmployer)
       to (number of (list of a among ev.agents such that a.id = employer.id)))

## `citizenship_(X), agent_(X,Employee), patient_(X,"usa")`, counted.
declaration us_citizen_ways content integer
  depends on world content W.World, employee content W.Entity
  equals
    Integer.sum of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events
         such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Citizenship)
       to ((number of (list of a among ev.agents such that a.id = employee.id))
           * (number of (list of q among ev.patients
                         such that q.tag = W.EntityTag.UsaEntity))))

declaration abroad_ways content integer
  depends on world content W.World, employer content W.Entity, employee content W.Entity
  equals
    (foreign_ways of world)
    * (american_employer_ways of world, employer)
    * (us_citizen_ways of world, employee)
```

## (c) Employment — the exclusions applied

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Excluded:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  ## Everything `s3306_c` excludes except paragraph (1), which differs between
  ## the two levels and so stays with the caller.
  output holds content boolean
  ## s3306_c_2/3, its guard alone — see "Cutting the two cycles" above.
  output domestic_excluded content boolean
```

```catala
scope Excluded:
  definition domestic_excluded equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
      and (is_domestic of world, ev)
      and (number of ev.patients) > 0
      and (exists g among ev.places such that is_private_setting of g)

  definition holds equals
    domestic_excluded
    or (output of ExclFamily with {
          -- world: world -- child_of: child_of -- service: service
          -- agent: employee -- patient: employer
          -- workday: workday }).holds
    or (output of ExclUsGovernment with {
          -- world: world -- service: service }).holds
    or (output of ExclState with {
          -- world: world -- service: service -- employer: Absent }).holds
    or (output of ExclStudent with {
          -- world: world -- injections: injections
          -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
          -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
          -- service: service -- employer: employer -- employee: employee
          -- workday: workday }).holds
    or (output of ExclForeignGovernment with {
          -- world: world -- service: service -- employer: employer }).holds
    or (output of ExclStudentNurse with {
          -- world: world -- service: service -- employer: employer
          -- employee: employee -- workday: workday }).holds
    or (output of ExclInternationalOrganization with {
          -- world: world -- service: service -- employer: employer }).holds
    or (output of ExclPenalInstitution with {
          -- world: world -- service: service -- employee: employee
          -- workday: workday }).holds
```

## Injected employment

Eight cases add a *clause* for `s3306_c/5` rather than facts — one of them
generates twelve workdays and their employees out of a `member/2` over a list.
The grounder expands each into rows, and they enter here as extra solutions
alongside the derived ones, exactly as an extra Prolog clause would.

```catala-metadata
declaration injected_employment content list of Emp
  depends on injections content list of W.Injection,
             service content optional of W.Entity,
             employer content optional of W.Entity,
             employee content optional of W.Entity,
             workday content optional of date,
             caly content optional of integer
  equals
    map each inj among
      (W.injections_for of injections, P.pred_s3306_c_5,
        [(key_of of service); (key_of of employer); (key_of of employee);
         (date_key_of of workday); (num_key_of of caly)])
    to Emp {
      -- service: ent_from of (W.injection_entity of inj, 1), service
      -- employer: ent_from of (W.injection_entity of inj, 2), employer
      -- employee: ent_from of (W.injection_entity of inj, 3), employee
      -- workday:
           (match (W.injection_date of inj, 4) with pattern
            -- Present content d: Present content d
            -- Absent: workday)
      -- caly:
           (match (W.injection_num of inj, 5) with pattern
            -- Present content n: Present content n
            -- Absent: caly) }
```

## (c) Employment — the inner level

```catala-metadata
declaration scope EmploymentCandidates:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  ## s3306_c_A/3 — performed in the United States
  output from_a content list of Emp
  ## s3306_c_B/4 — performed abroad by a US citizen for an American employer
  output from_b content list of Emp
  output every content list of Emp
  output holds_a content boolean
  output holds_b content boolean

declaration scope EmploymentLower:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  input caly content optional of integer
  ## The calendar year the clause actually uses: named by the caller, unless a
  ## workday was named, in which case it is that day's year.
  output effective_caly content optional of integer
  output solutions content list of Emp
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope EmploymentCandidates:
  definition from_a equals
    flatten_emp of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events such that ent_ok of service, e.ident)
       to (flatten_emp of
            (map each a among (ent_hits of employee, ev.agents)
             to (flatten_emp of
                  (map each p among (ent_hits of employer, ev.patients)
                   to (flatten_emp of
                        (map each g among (places_of of ev)
                         to (repeat_emp of
                               Emp { -- service: ev.ident -- employer: p
                                     -- employee: a -- workday: Absent
                                     -- caly: Absent },
                               (usa_ways of world, g)))))))))

  definition from_b equals
    flatten_emp of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among world.events such that ent_ok of service, e.ident)
       to (flatten_emp of
            (map each a among (ent_hits of employee, ev.agents)
             to (flatten_emp of
                  (map each p among (ent_hits of employer, ev.patients)
                   to (repeat_emp of
                         Emp { -- service: ev.ident -- employer: p
                               -- employee: a -- workday: Absent
                               -- caly: Absent },
                         (abroad_ways of world, p, a)))))))

  definition every equals from_a ++ from_b

  definition holds_a equals (number of from_a) > 0

  definition holds_b equals (number of from_b) > 0

scope EmploymentLower:
  definition effective_caly equals
    match workday with pattern
    -- Present content d: Present content (Date.get_year of d)
    -- Absent: caly

  definition solutions equals
    (if (caly_conflict of workday, caly)
        # A grant made without `discontiguous` replaces (c) and the derived
        # solutions are gone. See D69.
        or (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s3306_c_5) then [] else
      (list of e among
         (output of EmploymentCandidates with {
            -- world: world -- service: service
            -- employer: employer -- employee: employee }).every
       such that
         (exists ev among world.events such that
            ev.ident.id = e.service.id and ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service)
         and not (output of AgriculturalExcluded with {
                    -- world: world -- service: Present content e.service
                    -- caly: effective_caly
                    # This is the lower level: `s3306_c_1_A_ii` is
                    # `s3306_a_2_B`, which asks (c) back. See "Cutting the two
                    # cycles"; here it is hardwired false.
                    -- agri_employers: [] }).holds
         and not (output of Excluded with {
                    -- world: world -- injections: injections
                    -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                    -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                    -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                    -- service: Present content e.service
                    -- employer: Present content e.employer
                    -- employee: Present content e.employee
                    -- workday: workday }).holds))
    ++ (injected_employment of injections, service, employer, employee,
          workday, caly)

  definition holds equals (number of solutions) > 0
```

## (c)(1) as a whole, and the upper level of (c)

```catala-metadata
## `s3306_c` unifies its `Caly` argument with the year of its `Workday` when
## the caller named one. If the caller named both and they disagree, the clause
## has no solutions.
declaration caly_conflict content boolean
  depends on workday content optional of date, caly content optional of integer
  equals
    match workday with pattern
    -- Absent: false
    -- Present content d:
        (match caly with pattern
         -- Absent: false
         -- Present content y: y != (Date.get_year of d))

## An employer who satisfies (a)(2)(B) in a given calendar year. Threaded into
## (c)(1)(A)(ii) from outside so that (c) and (a)(2) stay a DAG.
declaration structure AgriYear:
  data employer content W.Entity
  data caly content integer

declaration scope AgriculturalExcluded:
  input world content W.World
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input caly content optional of integer
  input agri_employers content list of AgriYear
  ## s3306_c_1_A/3
  output subparagraph_a content boolean
  ## s3306_c_1/2
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope Employment:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input agri_employers content list of AgriYear
  input service content optional of W.Entity
  input employer content optional of W.Entity
  input employee content optional of W.Entity
  input workday content optional of date
  input caly content optional of integer
  output effective_caly content optional of integer
  ## s3306_c/5
  output solutions content list of Emp
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope AgriculturalExcluded:
  # Guarded on the agricultural-labor test that `holds` applies anyway, so
  # that the $20,000 findall below is not evaluated for every service in the
  # world: `and` is not lazy, but `if` is.
  definition subparagraph_a equals
    if not (exists ev among world.events such that
              (ent_ok of service, ev.ident) and (is_agricultural of world, ev))
    then false
    else
    match caly with pattern
    -- Absent: false
    -- Present content y:
        exists ev among world.events such that
          ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service
          and (ent_ok of service, ev.ident)
          and (exists p among ev.patients such that
                 (output of AgriculturalWages with {
                    -- world: world -- employer: Present content p
                    -- caly: y }).holds
                 or (exists ay among agri_employers such that
                       ay.employer.id = p.id and ay.caly = y))

  definition holds equals
    (exists ev among world.events such that
       (ent_ok of service, ev.ident) and (is_agricultural of world, ev))
    and not (subparagraph_a
             and (output of AgriculturalAlien with {
                    -- world: world -- service: service }).holds)

scope Employment:
  definition effective_caly equals
    match workday with pattern
    -- Present content d: Present content (Date.get_year of d)
    -- Absent: caly

  definition solutions equals
    (if (caly_conflict of workday, caly)
        # A grant made without `discontiguous` replaces (c) and the derived
        # solutions are gone. See D69.
        or (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s3306_c_5) then [] else
      (list of e among
         (output of EmploymentCandidates with {
            -- world: world -- service: service
            -- employer: employer -- employee: employee }).every
       such that
         (exists ev among world.events such that
            ev.ident.id = e.service.id and ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Service)
         and not (output of AgriculturalExcluded with {
                    -- world: world -- service: Present content e.service
                    -- caly: effective_caly
                    -- agri_employers: agri_employers }).holds
         and not (output of Excluded with {
                    -- world: world -- injections: injections
                    -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                    -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                    -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                    -- service: Present content e.service
                    -- employer: Present content e.employer
                    -- employee: Present content e.employee
                    -- workday: workday }).holds))
    ++ (injected_employment of injections, service, employer, employee,
          workday, caly)

  definition holds equals (number of solutions) > 0
```

## (a)(1)(B) and (a)(2)(B): ten days in ten different weeks

Both paragraphs collect the days somebody was employed, keep those falling in
the calendar year or the one before it, and demand ten distinct days spread
over ten distinct calendar weeks.

Neither can ever fire on a purely derived world. `s3306_c` reads its `Workday`
argument and never binds it, so the `findall` generator leaves `Day` unbound
and the `is_before` that follows fails. The days come from cases that inject a
clause for `s3306_c/5` — which is exactly the shape of the eight cases that do.

```catala-metadata
## s3306_a_1_is_day_of_employment/3 — a day of non-agricultural,
## non-domestic employment.
declaration scope GeneralDays:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input employer content W.Entity
  output days content list of date
  output employees content list of W.Entity

## s3306_a_2_is_day_of_employment/4 — five or more individuals in agricultural
## labor on one day.
declaration scope AgriDay:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input employer content W.Entity
  input at content date
  output individuals content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope EmployerDays:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input employer content W.Entity
  input caly content integer
  ## The candidate days, before the ten-day and ten-week tests.
  output workdays content list of date
  output employees content list of W.Entity
  ## s3306_a_1_B/4
  output holds_general content boolean
  ## s3306_a_2_B/6 — the agricultural variant, five individuals a day
  output agri_workdays content list of date
  output agri_employees content list of W.Entity
  output holds_agricultural content boolean
```

```catala
scope GeneralDays:
  definition days equals
    map each e among
      (list of x among
        (output of EmploymentLower with {
           -- world: world -- injections: injections
           -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
           -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
           -- service: Absent -- employer: Present content employer
           -- employee: Absent -- workday: Absent -- caly: Absent }).solutions
       such that
         (match x.workday with pattern -- Absent: false -- Present content d: true)
         and not ((is_agricultural_id of world, x.service)
                  or (is_domestic_id of world, x.service)))
    to (match e.workday with pattern
        -- Present content d: d
        -- Absent: |0001-01-01|)

  definition employees equals
    map each e among
      (list of x among
        (output of EmploymentLower with {
           -- world: world -- injections: injections
           -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
           -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
           -- service: Absent -- employer: Present content employer
           -- employee: Absent -- workday: Absent -- caly: Absent }).solutions
       such that
         (match x.workday with pattern -- Absent: false -- Present content d: true)
         and not ((is_agricultural_id of world, x.service)
                  or (is_domestic_id of world, x.service)))
    to e.employee

scope AgriDay:
  definition individuals equals
    dedup_entities of
      (map each e among
        (list of x among
          (output of EmploymentLower with {
             -- world: world -- injections: injections
             -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
             -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
             -- service: Absent -- employer: Present content employer
             -- employee: Absent -- workday: Present content at
             -- caly: Absent }).solutions
         such that is_agricultural_id of world, x.service)
       to e.employee)

  definition holds equals (number of individuals) >= 5

scope EmployerDays:
  definition workdays equals
    list of d among
      (output of GeneralDays with {
         -- world: world -- injections: injections
         -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
         -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
         -- employer: employer }).days
    such that (W.first_day_year of (caly - 1)) <= d and d <= (W.last_day_year of caly)

  definition employees equals
    (output of GeneralDays with {
       -- world: world -- injections: injections
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- employer: employer }).employees

  definition holds_general equals
    (number of (dedup_dates of workdays)) >= 10
    and (number of (dedup_ints of (map each d among workdays to (week_of of d)))) >= 10

  definition agri_workdays equals
    list of d among
      (dedup_dates of
        (map each e among
          (list of x among
            (output of EmploymentLower with {
               -- world: world -- injections: injections
               -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
               -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
               -- service: Absent -- employer: Present content employer
               -- employee: Absent -- workday: Absent -- caly: Absent }).solutions
           such that
             (match x.workday with pattern -- Absent: false -- Present content d: true))
         to (match e.workday with pattern
             -- Present content d: d
             -- Absent: |0001-01-01|)))
    such that
      (W.first_day_year of (caly - 1)) <= d and d <= (W.last_day_year of caly)
      and (output of AgriDay with {
             -- world: world -- injections: injections
             -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
             -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
             -- employer: employer -- at: d }).holds

  definition agri_employees equals
    flatten_entities of
      (map each d among agri_workdays
       to (output of AgriDay with {
             -- world: world -- injections: injections
             -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
             -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
             -- employer: employer -- at: d }).individuals)

  definition holds_agricultural equals
    (number of agri_workdays) >= 10
    and (number of (dedup_ints of (map each d among agri_workdays to (week_of of d)))) >= 10
```

## (b) Wages

`s3306_b/8` is the section's other generator, and the one §3301 sums. Every
goal in its conjunction that can match more than one fact multiplies the row,
because `findall`+`sum_list` counts solutions: a payment carrying two
`amount_` rows is counted twice, and so is one paid in two media.

```catala-metadata
declaration structure WageRow:
  data wages content money
  data remuneration content W.Entity
  data employment content W.Entity
  data payer content W.Entity
  data payee content W.Entity
  data employer content W.Entity
  data employee content W.Entity

declaration flatten_wage content list of WageRow
  depends on nested content list of list of WageRow
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

declaration repeat_wage content list of WageRow
  depends on r content WageRow, n content integer
  equals map each i among (List.sequence of 1, (n + 1)) to r

## `((\+ means_(R,_)) ; means_(R,Medium))` with `Medium` unbound: one solution
## when the payment names no medium, otherwise one per medium named.
declaration medium_ways content integer
  depends on r content W.Event
  equals if (number of r.media) = 0 then 1 else (number of r.media)

declaration is_plan content boolean
  depends on world content W.World, e content W.Entity
  equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.ident.id = e.id and ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.Plan

declaration beneficiaries_of content list of W.Entity
  depends on world content W.World, e content W.Entity
  equals
    flatten_entities of
      (map each ev among (list of x among world.events such that x.ident.id = e.id)
       to ev.beneficiaries)

## `(patient_(R,Payee), \+ plan_(Payee)) ; (patient_(R,Plan), plan_(Plan),
## beneficiary_(Plan,Payee))` -- a payment made to somebody, or into a plan
## somebody benefits from.
declaration structure PayeeRow:
  data payee content W.Entity
  data plan content optional of W.Entity

declaration flatten_payee content list of PayeeRow
  depends on nested content list of list of PayeeRow
  equals combine all inner among nested in acc initially [] with acc ++ inner

declaration payee_rows content list of PayeeRow
  depends on world content W.World, r content W.Event
  equals
    (map each q among (list of x among r.patients such that not (is_plan of world, x))
     to PayeeRow { -- payee: q -- plan: Absent })
    ++ (flatten_payee of
         (map each pl among (list of x among r.patients such that is_plan of world, x)
          to (map each b among (beneficiaries_of of world, pl)
              to PayeeRow { -- payee: b -- plan: Present content pl })))

## `end_(E,T)` for an event named by id rather than held in hand.
declaration ends_of content list of date
  depends on world content W.World, e content W.Entity
  equals
    flatten_dates of
      (map each ev among (list of x among world.events such that x.ident.id = e.id)
       to ev.ends)

## The event ids in a role, so an `\+` can be written over them.
declaration events_with_kind content list of W.Event
  depends on world content W.World, k content W.EventKind
  equals list of e among world.events such that e.kinds contains k
```

### (b)(2), (b)(7), (b)(10), (b)(11) and (b)(15): what wages are not

